  "details": "The new update has caused group names to become shortened/culled very inconsistently across different contexts - artificially limiting the name length without any standard.\n\nThis happens when it could otherwise be avoided by having the group name on it's own line.\n\nExample group name: Order of the Broken Beats\n\n- 25 characters long\n\n- Nameplate - shortening amount varies depending on the amount of user settings (earmuff, mute, etc.) - Why not have the icons on the right moved above/below to allow it to always show the full group name?\n\n- Bio - always shortens to 16 characters - \"Order of the Bro...\" - despite there being enough room available on the right. This is to account for variable pronoun length, but it could also be moved below above or below pronoun to allow any group name length.\n\n- Main profile group list - shortens to 22 characters -\"Order of the Broken Be...\". This one is fair enough, maybe could auto shrink font instead to fit?",
